{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And the fish, etc., died.</b> The intention in this is to tell that they had a sign in this deed — for it was not the deed of demons (shedim) nor the deed of sorcerers, since the deed of these two would be mere appearance and not actual reality, and the appearance would be only to the eyes of the beholders, not that it would be actual blood that would kill all who drank of it, even fish. Therefore it says <b>and the fish</b>, etc., <b>died, and the river stank</b> — and this would be for them an everlasting sign that the deed of Elohim it is, a true act and not mere appearance. Further, it says <b>and the blood was throughout all the land of Egypt</b>, etc. — for even in the bathhouses and in the pools. Or perhaps it further intends to say that that blood which was made from the water — even though they would take it from one place and put it in another place and repeat, etc. — whereas any thing that comes from the deed of demons (shedim), a change of place annuls it, especially when they set it upon the earth, as is known (Zohar 2:190a) — but in our case the blood remained in its existence throughout all the land of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:42.005431879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}